-- ============================================================================
-- Migration 58 DOWN: no-op (made non-destructive in O.2a).
--
-- Migration 58 is now a self-healing schema/data repair: it deletes only
-- null-endpoint junk rows and re-asserts the canonical `relation` TYPE RELATION
-- definition (migration 39) with OVERWRITE. There is no faithful inverse —
--   * the deleted rows were malformed legacy junk (null in/out), not real data
--     worth restoring; and
--   * the previous down (`REMOVE TABLE IF EXISTS relation`) was itself
--     DESTRUCTIVE: rolling back would wipe every real edge created since the
--     table was healthy, which defeats the whole point of the non-destructive
--     rewrite.
-- Down intentionally does nothing; mirrors the migration 61 / 62 down
-- convention. The canonical relation definition lives in migration 39 and is
-- re-asserted by 39 / 58 / 62 on any forward run.
-- ============================================================================
